---
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";

const host = "https://api.emojisense.com";
const pack = `${host}/v1/pack/0.1.0`;

const installReact = "npm install @emojisense/react frimousse";

const frimousse = `import { useEmojisense } from "@emojisense/react";
import { EmojisensePicker } from "@emojisense/react/frimousse";

export function EmojiButton({ onPick }: { onPick: (emoji: string) => void }) {
  const sense = useEmojisense({
    packBaseUrl: "${pack}",
    endpoint: "${host}",
    publishableKey: "pk_live_…",
  });

  return <EmojisensePicker emojisense={sense} onEmojiSelect={({ emoji }) => onPick(emoji)} />;
}`;

const hooks = `import { useEmojiSearch, useEmojisense } from "@emojisense/react";

const sense = useEmojisense({ packBaseUrl, endpoint, publishableKey });
const { results, status } = useEmojiSearch(query, sense, { limit: 24 });
// results: [{ emoji: "🚀", id: "1F680", score: 0.9, source: "alias" }, …]`;

const installCore = "npm install emojisense";

const vanilla = `import { createEngine, loadPacks } from "emojisense";

const engine = createEngine(await loadPacks({ baseUrl: "${pack}" }));
engine.search("ship it").results;
// [{ emoji: "🚢", id: "1F6A2", score: …, source: "alias" }, { emoji: "🚀", … }, …]`;

const session = `import {
  chainProviders,
  createSearchSession,
  createSemanticClient,
  createShardProvider,
} from "emojisense";

const session = createSearchSession({
  engine,
  // Cheapest first: precomputed shards (free static files), then the API.
  semantic: chainProviders(
    createShardProvider({ baseUrl: "${host}/p/0.1.0" }),
    createSemanticClient({ endpoint: "${host}", key: "pk_live_…" }),
  ),
  onChange: (state) => render(state.results),
});

input.addEventListener("input", () => session.update(input.value));`;

const installWebComponent = "npm install @emojisense/web-component";

const webComponent = `<script type="module">
  import "@emojisense/web-component";
</script>

<emojisense-picker
  pack-base-url="${pack}"
  endpoint="${host}"
  publishable-key="pk_live_…"
></emojisense-picker>

<script type="module">
  document
    .querySelector("emojisense-picker")
    .addEventListener("emoji-select", (event) => insert(event.detail.emoji));
</script>`;
---

<Docs path="/docs/" source="README.md">
  <h2 id="before-you-start">Before you start</h2>
  <p>You need two URLs and, for production, one key:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>Pack base URL</strong>: where the data packs live, for example <code>{pack}</code>.</li>
    <li><strong>Endpoint</strong>: the search API. Leave it out for offline search with the dictionary only.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Publishable key</strong> (<code>pk_live_…</code>): from the dashboard, bound to your site’s
      origins. Without a key, the API applies a stricter anonymous rate limit.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    Search starts as soon as the English core pack (about 180 KB compressed) arrives. The extension pack
    with more aliases and typos loads when the browser is idle.
  </p>

  <h2 id="react-frimousse">React and Frimousse</h2>
  <p>
    The adapter keeps the Frimousse browse view. As soon as someone types, Emojisense ranks the results,
    with the same <code>onEmojiSelect</code> contract and skin tone.
  </p>
  <pre class="code"><code>{installReact}</code></pre>
  <pre class="code"><code>{frimousse}</code></pre>
  <p>
    Style it like any Frimousse picker. The results grid adds <code>[data-emojisense-results]</code> and
    <code>[data-active]</code> hooks.
  </p>

  <h3 id="hooks-only">Your own picker UI</h3>
  <p>
    Use the hooks directly. Dictionary results update on every keystroke. Semantic results arrive a moment
    later and merge in without moving confident hits.
  </p>
  <pre class="code"><code>{hooks}</code></pre>

  <h2 id="vanilla">Plain JavaScript</h2>
  <p>
    The core engine has no dependencies. It runs in browsers, Node, Deno, Bun, Workers and extensions.
  </p>
  <pre class="code"><code>{installCore}</code></pre>
  <pre class="code"><code>{vanilla}</code></pre>
  <p>For search as you type, with semantic results when the dictionary is unsure, use a search session:</p>
  <pre class="code"><code>{session}</code></pre>

  <h2 id="web-component">Web component</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;emojisense-picker&gt;</code> works in Vue, Svelte, Angular and plain HTML. It is in progress: the
    attribute and event names below can change before the first release.
  </p>
  <pre class="code"><code>{installWebComponent}</code></pre>
  <pre class="code"><code>{webComponent}</code></pre>

  <h2 id="next">Next steps</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><a href="/docs/api/">HTTP API</a>: endpoints, keys, metering and status codes.</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/pack-format/">Pack format</a>: port the engine to Swift, Kotlin or anything else.</li>
    <li><a href="/docs/self-host/">Self-host</a>: run the API on your own Cloudflare account.</li>
    <li><a href="/pricing/">Pricing</a>: what is free and what the plans add.</li>
  </ul>
</Docs>
